{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS5edhJnPt96hDHNmiPm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Connect flow now works end to end against a local fake of Intervals.icu. I have not tested against the real service, so the duplicate-scope cause is inferred, not confirmed. The changes are in `server.py`, `config.py` and `static/app.js`, uncommitted. The causes and the reasoning for each are in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**Causes**\n1. **Connect always 401s.** The button was a plain link to a GET route that needs the `Authorization` header, and a page navigation doesn't send it. Init is now a POST that returns `{authorize_url}` as JSON, and the button calls it with `fetch` and navigates.\n2. **Scope string repeats areas.** `ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE` and `CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE` were both present. Since the calendar sync shipped on 10-02, the authorize step fails. The scope is now `ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`. The logs show `invalid_request` without naming the scope, so the duplicate-area cause is my inference from timing.\n3. **A fake one-hour expiry.** The token response has no `expires_in`, so the code defaulted to 3600 s. The refresher then marked the athlete \"expired, reconnect\" an hour later, which is the Rivera report. I removed the expiry logic and the refresh machinery, since Intervals issues no refresh tokens.\n4. **Revocation not detected.** A 401 from Intervals now clears the token and shows the reconnect prompt.\n\n**Colleague's note:** I applied the init-as-POST fix, the one-area-per-scope rule, the no-expiry and lazy-401 handling, and the athlete-id-from-response point (which was already in place). I did not remove `grant_type` and `redirect_uri` from the token exchange, because the real provider accepted them in the September log. I did not switch state to a JWT, because the existing HMAC state already covers this case. I did not add the account-mismatch guard, since it isn't one of these causes. Encryption at rest isn't implemented, because this repo's store is in memory.\n\n**Verification:** Against a local fake provider, the original code returned 401 for the GET and \"Duplicate scope\" on authorize. After the change, POST init returns the authorize URL and the callback connects. Wellness returns 200, and after a simulated revoke it returns 409 with status `expired, reconnect`. I did not contact intervals.icu or deploy anything.\n\n**Still needs a real check:**\n- Whether live Intervals accepts the new scope string.\n- Whether the registered `redirect_uri` matches `http://localhost:8766/api/intervals/callback`.\n- Real revocation behaviour.\n\nAthletes will need to reconnect once after deploy, and `APP_SECRET` and `CLIENT_SECRET` should move out of `config.py`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":260,"cache_read_input_tokens":61992,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":260},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d1e5ae0e-d0d2-4440-8edd-db12ef6e486f","uuid":"2414be80-eb9d-483c-adbc-6cf1c3cb361d","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:05:46.479Z","request_id":"req_011CgS5edSvtEv1dVX4VXuGQ"}
